# forge.hex1 — Phase 3: the Forge language engine, written in hex1 assembly (hand-typed x86-64 opcodes).
#
# The engine is a subroutine-threaded compiler + interpreter for a Forth-style language.
#   - Dynamic memory: at startup it mmaps a 64 MB RWX data space at 0x10000000 (dict, stacks, buffers),
#     and ALLOT/HERE/VARIABLE let programs claim more of it at run time.
#   - Arbitrary control flow: IF/ELSE/THEN, BEGIN/UNTIL, BEGIN/WHILE/REPEAT, DO/LOOP (+I, UNLOOP),
#     recursion, EXIT (early return) — all compiled to native machine code.
#   - FFI: the SYSCALL word issues raw Linux kernel syscalls with 6 register arguments; EXECUTE calls
#     any code address; @/!/C@/C! read and write raw memory.
# Register conventions: r13=LATEST (dict head) r12=HERE (data-space pointer) r14=PSP (data stack, grows down)
#   rbx=CSP (compiler control stack, grows down) rbp=STATE (0=interpret, 1=compile). Primitives only
#   use rax/rcx/rdx/rsi/rdi/r8-r11, so engine registers survive words and syscalls.
# Data-space layout (256 MB mmap at 0x10000000):
#   0x10000000 dict+code+data grows up (to 0x1C000000, 192 MB) | 0x1C000000 PSP top | 0x1C100000 CSP top |
#   0x1C200000 line buffer (64 KB) | 0x1C210000 token buffer | 0x1C211000 number buffer | 0x1C212000 emit buffer |
#   0x1C212100 INPTR 0x1C212108 INEND 0x1C212110 TOKLEN 0x1C212118 SSTRPTR 0x1C212120 INFILE 0x1C212128 SRCFILL
#   0x1C212130 SRCBASE 0x1C212138 SAVEDRSP | 0x1C300000 string area (8 MB) | 0x1D000000 source-file buffer (48 MB).
#
# ---- ELF64 header (entry 0x400078) ----
7f 45 4c 46 02 01 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
02 00 3e 00 01 00 00 00
78 00 40 00 00 00 00 00
40 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00
40 00 38 00 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
01 00 00 00 07 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 40 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 40 00 00 00 00 00
@ 00 00 00 00                   ; p_filesz (low half from @, high half zero)
@ 00 00 00 00                   ; p_memsz
00 10 00 00 00 00 00 00
# ---- code ----
# ---- variables (cells in the data space) ----
#   INPTR 0x1C212100  INEND 0x1C212108  TOKLEN 0x1C212110  SSTRPTR 0x1C212118  INFILE 0x1C212120
#   SRCFILL 0x1C212128  SRCBASE 0x1C212130  REPLRSP 0x1C212138  ARGI 0x1C212140  ENTRYRSP 0x1C212148
